description:
Turn a Process Monitor capture saved as CSV (lesson 3.04) into the summary you would write by hand:

```cpp
struct Event { std::string time, process, pid, operation, path, result, detail; };
struct Summary
{
    std::vector<std::string> filesRead, filesWritten, keysRead, keysWritten, notFound;
};

std::vector<std::string> splitCsvLine(const std::string& line);
std::vector<Event> parseLog(const std::string& csv);
Summary summarise(const std::vector<Event>& events, const std::string& process);
```

- **splitCsvLine** splits one CSV line into fields. Fields may be wrapped in double quotes; inside quotes, commas are part of the field and `""` stands for one `"`.
- **parseLog** skips the header line and blank lines and turns each other line of 7 fields into an `Event` (lines with a different number of fields are skipped).
- **summarise** looks only at events of `process` and fills each list with **distinct** paths, sorted:
  - `filesRead`: operation `ReadFile` with result `SUCCESS`;
  - `filesWritten`: operation `WriteFile` with result `SUCCESS`;
  - `keysRead`: `RegQueryValue` with result `SUCCESS`;
  - `keysWritten`: `RegSetValue` with result `SUCCESS`;
  - `notFound`: any operation with result `NAME NOT FOUND`.

